# Release tag signers (Round 34, R33-9). Read by .github/workflows/release.yml
# through .github/scripts/release-gate.sh: a `v*` tag is released only when it
# is an annotated tag SSH-signed (git tag -s, gpg.format=ssh) by a key listed
# here, on a commit that is on main and passed the CI gate of a push to main.
#
# OWNER: THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY. Until a key is added below, EVERY
# release fails closed at the gate ("names no signer"). Add your release
# signing key (docs/ops/production-checklist.md, "Release integrity"), one line
# per key, in ssh-keygen's allowed_signers format:
#
#   <your git email> namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
#
# and change this file only through a reviewed pull request to main.
#
# Validity windows (Round 38, D2-5): a line may bound when its key may sign a
# release, in ssh-keygen's allowed_signers options, judged at release time
# (never by the tag's own, signer-chosen date):
#
#   <email> namespaces="git",valid-after="20261101",valid-before="20271101" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
#
# Revocation: add the key's public line to .github/revoked_signers (a revoked
# key is refused even while it is listed here and inside its window), and in
# the same pull request delete its line here or end it with valid-before.
# release-guard.yml applies main's copy of both files to every release run,
# tags on older commits included.
